    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n**What the spec needed:** when an owner is created and later read back, the JSON must expose `displayName` formatted exactly as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` from the stored names.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the field from the stored entity:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the read responder (`RespondWithOwner`) go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, `displayName` is derived consistently from the persisted `Owner`. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite report `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
